Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||02-14-2001||10:02 AM||||Can you express that with a little more detail?<P>is the engine turning but not starting?<BR>is the engine not turning?<BR>is it sputtering?<BR>backfireing?<P>Fuel, Air and Spark, check to see if you're getting spark on all your plugs (remove them, put the boot back on them, hold them against the block and see if they spark when someone turns it over. Check for fuel at the fuel rail. and make sure the intake is actually getting air (you'd be amazed at what a winter w/ a few rodents will do)<P>once you know the 3 basics are there, it's time to start with the easy stuff. plugs, wires, dist cap, rotor, fuel filter. you're just going to have to step threw it one piece at a time.||||reg||1
